 {"attempt_id": "C0018-A001", "author": "claude-probability-1000-continue-0907", "correction_note": "The existence-of-exponent claim assumed alpha_4(rho,R) depends on R/rho only up to constants (scale invariance up to constants), which is unproved on Z^2; see C0018-A002.", "independent_check": "The de Bruijn-Erdos approximate subadditivity lemma requires |f(xy)-f(x)-f(y)| bounded, which is exactly the quasi-multiplicativity statement with r=1 scaled; no gap found.", "key_identity": "Quasi-multiplicativity => approximate subadditivity of -log alpha_4 in log R => the limit exponent exists on Z^2.", "method": "Subadditivity of arm probabilities under quasi-multiplicativity.", "obstruction": "The value 5/4 requires conformal invariance on Z^2.", "problem_id": "C0018", "recorded_at": "2026-09-07T06:38:45Z", "result": "Quasi-multiplicativity alpha_4(r,R) asymp alpha_4(r,rho) alpha_4(rho,R) holds on Z^2 by RSW, which makes -log alpha_4(1,R) approximately subadditive in log R up to additive constants; Fekete's lemma then gives existence of the limit of -log alpha_4(1,R)/log R PROVIDED the additive constant is bounded, which it is, so the exponent xi_4 EXISTS on Z^2 as a limit in the sense lim -log alpha_4(R)/log R. Checked: quasi-multiplicativity with constants C^{-1} <= alpha(r,R)/(alpha(r,rho) alpha(rho,R)) <= C gives |f(R) - f(r) - f(R/r)| <= log C for f = -log alpha_4, and a function with this property has f(R)/log R convergent (approximate subadditivity, de Bruijn-Erdos). So existence of the exponent is not the open part; the open part is the value 5/4, which depends on conformal invariance (C0017) or an independent computation. The universal bounds available are xi_4 in (1, 2) from the 5-arm exponent 2 and the monotone-coupling comparison alpha_4 <= alpha_2 ... giving xi_4 > xi_2 >= ... ; I did not improve them.", "schema": "probability-attempt.v1", "substantive": true, "superseded_by": "C0018-A002"}
